# =====================================================================================
# bridge_neg.ttl — the FAILING NEGATIVE fixture for BridgeShape (W2 · SP0, T-FIX).
# The materialized RED (D24: sh:conforms true alone is vacuous — a positive AND a failing
# negative per shape).
# =====================================================================================
# A rec:denotatum:record minted WITHOUT its fnd: retire bridge — it carries NO skos:exactMatch /
# skos:closeMatch edge (either direction) to a urn:silmaril:fnd: legacy name (the SINGLE injected
# violation; the positive twin fixtures/bridge_pos.ttl carries the skos:exactMatch). Merged onto
# the algebra data graph the graph MUST NOT conform: BridgeShape's sh:sparql FILTER NOT EXISTS
# (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl:250) returns this focus, so an inbound SP1/SP2/SP3 fnd:* reference
# would not resolve through the fold. It carries identifier/notation ONLY (NO provenance) and a
# single record-ladder type, so V1DenotatumHygieneShape stays satisfied and exactly BridgeShape
# flips conforms True->False.
#
# Depth-gate compliance: the subject is an owl:NamedIndividual with a SPECIFIC type
# (rec:denotatum:record), never an owl:Class.

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rel:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:relation:> .
@prefix rec:  <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:grounding:ontology:basic:formal:domain:knowledge:representation:kingdom:specification:phylum:formal:contract:class:class:order:declared:family:seed:genus:registry:species:> .

# --- a denotatum with NO fnd: retire bridge (INVALID: inbound fnd:* would not resolve) ---
<urn:silmaril:fixture:algebra:bridge:negative>
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:denotatum:record ;
    rel:notation   "denotatum MISSING its fnd: retire bridge (INJECTED VIOLATION)" ;
    rel:identifier "urn:silmaril:fixture:algebra:bridge:negative" .
    # INJECTED VIOLATION: no skos:exactMatch/closeMatch to a urn:silmaril:fnd: name -> BridgeShape RED
